{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And lodge.</b> Bring them into the house immediately, before the wanton men of the city set their eyes on you — for if you linger outside the house, perhaps they will recognize you." "<b>And wash your feet.</b> This too he did properly. He said: if these are seen with the dust on their feet, the wicked men will investigate where we lodged." "<b>And lodge, and wash.</b> Does a person normally lodge first and afterward wash? And furthermore, Abraham said to them first, 'and wash your feet.' Rather, this is what Lot said: if they enter the house after washing their feet, perhaps some of the wanton men of the city will recognize them and see their feet without dirt, and they will say: already three days have passed since these came to your house, and you did not inform us. It is better that they enter with their feet still soiled, and if their arrival is recognized, they will appear as people who just arrived. Therefore he said, 'and rise early and go on your way,' lest they recognize you." "<b>For in the square we lodge.</b> So that the people of the city see us — that we have come for its overturning; perhaps they will repent."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:50.500187410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}